{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018xRcTnwHNf8V6rsPRmZ4gP","type":"tool_result","content":"88:- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n545:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n1161:## 21d. Shell\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1605:- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\n1695:- `strategy.minimap(colors = {})` †: E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera\n80:- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n105:- 1675 Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays (engine/modules/strategy.js); E.Clock: clock, E.Strategy: strategy\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase). An alert guard that loses the target searches for forget seconds. Each step: suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)\n1003:- `suspicion.hear(strength, at)` †: a noise heard (strength 0..1, from E.hears) at a point: at least noticed, never more than searching\n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1014:- `E.hears(lis, noise, map)`: how loud a noise ({ x, y, z, loud: its radius in world units, 80 }) is where listener stands: 1 at the noise, 0 at its radius and beyond, halved when a top of map stands between them (a wall muffles it)\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.map, times the target's own exposure (default 1) and .6 when it crouches (it also shows lower). o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye }\n1677:- `new E.Clock(o = {}) → clock` †: new E.Clock({ day: 240 (real seconds of game time a day), hour: 8 (to start at) })\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181331__x22cc1b/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca45a593-66ad-492b-ba14-15d9cf0373b1","uuid":"2ba58ae2-1a7d-498f-a643-2a6a8d648f1e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:14:32.523Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"88:- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n545:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n1161:## 21d. Shell\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1605:- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\n1695:- `strategy.minimap(colors = {})` †: E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera\n80:- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n105:- 1675 Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays (engine/modules/strategy.js); E.Clock: clock, E.Strategy: strategy\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase). An alert guard that loses the target searches for forget seconds. Each step: suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)\n1003:- `suspicion.hear(strength, at)` †: a noise heard (strength 0..1, from E.hears) at a point: at least noticed, never more than searching\n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1014:- `E.hears(lis, noise, map)`: how loud a noise ({ x, y, z, loud: its radius in world units, 80 }) is where listener stands: 1 at the noise, 0 at its radius and beyond, halved when a top of map stands between them (a wall muffles it)\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.map, times the target's own exposure (default 1) and .6 when it crouches (it also shows lower). o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye }\n1677:- `new E.Clock(o = {}) → clock` †: new E.Clock({ day: 240 (real seconds of game time a day), hour: 8 (to start at) })","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181331__x22cc1b/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018xRcTnwHNf8V6rsPRmZ4gP","permission_decision